neoxify-patch header: ios-tcp-buffers

Caps the TUN inbound's per-connection TCP buffers in the iOS engine.
Written against xray-core v26.6.27 (45cf2898ab12), proxy/tun/stack_gvisor.go.
Applied by apps/mobile/scripts/xray-core-patch.sh, for the iOS build only.
Measured with TestEngineMemory (plugins/vpn/xray); see the journal,
2026-11-12. If it stops applying after a version bump, re-make it by
hand against the new stack_gvisor.go: the four sizes are the whole change.

--- a/proxy/tun/stack_gvisor.go
+++ b/proxy/tun/stack_gvisor.go
@@ -23,13 +23,20 @@
 const (
 	defaultNIC tcpip.NICID = 1
 
-	tcpRXBufMinSize = tcp.MinBufferSize
-	tcpRXBufDefSize = tcp.DefaultSendBufferSize
-	tcpRXBufMaxSize = 8 << 20 // 8MiB
-
-	tcpTXBufMinSize = tcp.MinBufferSize
-	tcpTXBufDefSize = tcp.DefaultReceiveBufferSize
-	tcpTXBufMaxSize = 6 << 20 // 6MiB
+	// neoxify-patch: ios-tcp-buffers. Every connection the phone opens
+	// is held in this stack, and a stalled one holds as much as these
+	// allow -- upstream, 8 MiB received and 6 MiB to send, per connection
+	// -- inside an iOS packet tunnel that is killed at about 50 MB. The
+	// phone's apps and this stack are one hop apart in memory, so a window
+	// this size does not limit a connection's speed; the real path's
+	// window belongs to the engine's own socket to the server.
+	tcpRXBufMinSize = tcp.MinBufferSize
+	tcpRXBufDefSize = 256 << 10
+	tcpRXBufMaxSize = 512 << 10
+
+	tcpTXBufMinSize = tcp.MinBufferSize
+	tcpTXBufDefSize = 256 << 10
+	tcpTXBufMaxSize = 512 << 10
 )
 
 // stackGVisor is ip stack implemented by gVisor package
